river connection has inadvertently introduced fresh ecological challenges that could disrupt local ecosystems.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1900-chicago-engineers-reversed-the-flow-of-an-entire-river-to-push-the-citys-sewage-away-from-lake-michigan-126-years-later-the-river-still-runs-backwards/articleshow/134122316.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1900-chicago-engineers-reversed-the-flow-of-an-entire-river-to-push-the-citys-sewage-away-from-lake-michigan-126-years-later-the-river-still-runs-backwards/articleshow/134122316.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-12T18:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134122862,imgsize-1261879.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists track nearly every cell in a living vertebrate at the same time]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134119222.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/scientists-built-a-system-that-watches-activity-across-nearly-every-cell-of-a-living-vertebrate-at-once-transparent-zebrafish-revealed-body-wide-signals-moving-between-organs/articleshow/134119222.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/scientists-built-a-system-that-watches-activity-across-nearly-every-cell-of-a-living-vertebrate-at-once-transparent-zebrafish-revealed-body-wide-signals-moving-between-organs/articleshow/134119222.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-12T17:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134119444,imgsize-846784.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2001, a guard saved 6 from the burning World Trade Center; 25 years later, they are trying to save him]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134115666.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A security guard who saved lives during 9/11 now battles kidney cancer. Dereck Lovell guided survivors through the South Tower's smoke and flames. He is now awaiting a kidney transplant after his own kidneys were removed. Survivors he rescued are raising awareness for his urgent need. Lovell, who considers himself a job doer, is now receiving help.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2001-a-security-guard-led-6-people-trapped-on-the-70th-floor-to-safety-as-the-world-trade-center-burned-25-years-later-the-survivors-he-saved-are-trying-to-save-his-life/articleshow/134115666.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2001-a-security-guard-led-6-people-trapped-on-the-70th-floor-to-safety-as-the-world-trade-center-burned-25-years-later-the-survivors-he-saved-are-trying-to-save-his-life/articleshow/134115666.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-12T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134116149,imgsize-1855774.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[For decades, scientists thought North America had a cheetah; DNA links it to pumas 2.6M years ago]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134120467.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a groundbreaking revelation, ancient DNA analysis has clarified that Miracinonyx trumani is more closely related to pumas than cheetahs. This extinct cat thrived in North America during the Pleistocene epoch and had the unique ability to fish in colder regions. While its structure suggested agility, evolutionary genetics indicated that convergence was at play, with low genetic variety likely contributing to its disappearance from the ecosystem.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/for-decades-scientists-thought-north-america-had-its-own-cheetah-ancient-dna-reveals-the-extinct-cat-split-from-the-puma-lineage-2-6-million-years-ago/articleshow/134120467.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/for-decades-scientists-thought-north-america-had-its-own-cheetah-ancient-dna-reveals-the-extinct-cat-split-from-the-puma-lineage-2-6-million-years-ago/articleshow/134120467.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-12T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134121130,imgsize-2249440.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[$29.5M New York estate heads to auction with bids starting at just $5M]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134116667.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/once-priced-at-29-5-million-a-151-acre-new-york-estate-is-now-going-to-auction-its-14000-sq-ft-mansion-could-sell-for-as-little-as-5-million/articleshow/134116667.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/once-priced-at-29-5-million-a-151-acre-new-york-estate-is-now-going-to-auction-its-14000-sq-ft-mansion-could-sell-for-as-little-as-5-million/articleshow/134116667.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-12T16:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134116813,imgsize-1001929.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[160-year-old St 